  "changed_since_previous": "Added `filter_c_flags` to `cmake/secp256k1.cmake` to compile-test hardening flags against the C compiler (accumulating previously accepted flags so `-U_FORTIFY_SOURCE` and `-D_FORTIFY_SOURCE=3` are tested together) before passing them to secp256k1.",
  "card": "This pull request passes Bitcoin Core's compiler and linker hardening flags to the embedded libsecp256k1 subtree by isolating them in a `hardening_interface` CMake target and testing them with the C compiler. Previously, secp256k1 objects were built without hardening options such as stack clash protection and branch protection. Because linkers drop binary-wide control-flow protection markers if even a single linked object lacks them, secp256k1 objects stripped these protections from release executables on modern toolchains. Testing on AArch64 with GCC 15 confirms that passing these flags restores BTI, PAC, and GCS binary feature properties on bitcoind.",
